The `config/admins.json` file is where you define who gets Administrator access in the portal (which gives them access to the Submission Tracker, HR Queries, Support Queries, etc.).

You should list the email addresses of all your admins in that file. Just make sure to format it like a list, separating each email with a comma, and wrapping the emails in quotes.

For example, you should replace `"[EMAIL_ADDRESS]"` with a real email, and it should look something like this:

```json
{
  "admins": [
    "gnanasree.ponnuru@gantecusa.com",
    "hemalatha.malem@gantecusa.com",
    "another.admin@gantecusa.com"
  ]
}
```

Once you save that file, the server will automatically detect those emails and grant those users Admin privileges when they log in!


When someone logs into the portal:
* **Admins** (the emails listed in your `admins.json` file) will see the **Submission Tracker** in their sidebar menu, which allows them to view HR and Support queries.
* **Standard Employees** (everyone else) will see all of the normal tools (like Leave, Holidays, Idea Hub, Contact HR, etc.) but the **Submission Tracker** will be completely hidden from their menu.

It dynamically adjusts the menu based on who is logged in!

